      "writtenOn": "2023-12-04T17:02:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t like string-based solutions, because they can be broken very easily. For example, there is no convention on what \"true\" value of boolean build flag is: it may be `true`, `True` or even `1`. And having only one flag using `GetBuildFlagBool` when all other flags use struct fields increases risks of breaking it without anyone noticing.\n\nIt is more reliable to use an existing framework for boolean build flags, namely `add_json_bool` in makefiles and golang JSON decoding, which will detect non-standard values, see https://go.dev/play/p/EyRzP1fqSQp.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "eb7ff0c3_e0589337",
